                <option value="injury">Injury</option>
                <option value="maternity">Maternity</option>
            </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field-container">
            <label for="details">Details:</label>
            <textarea id="details"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div class="field-container">
            <label for="documents">Upload Documents:</label>
            <input type="file" id="documents" multiple onchange="updateFileList()">
            <div id="file-list"></div>
        </div>
        <button type="submit">Submit Claim</button>
    </form>
    <div id="confirmation">
        <p>Reference Number: <span id="reference-number"></span></p>
        <p>Status: Received</p>
    </div>

    <footer>MapleSure Insurance — fictional demo application</footer>

    <script>
        (function trackView() {
            var analyticsElem = document.getElementById('analytics');
            analyticsElem.innerHTML = 'Page View Recorded';
            console.log('Analytics: Page View Recorded');
        })();

        function lookupMember() {
            // Mock data
            var members = {
                '123': 'John Doe, Employee',
                '456': 'Jane Smith, Employee'
            };
            var memberId = document.getElementById('member-id').value;
            var details = members[memberId] || 'Member not found';
            document.getElementById('member-details').innerText = details;
        }

        function updateFileList() {
            var input = document.getElementById('documents');
            var fileListDiv = document.getElementById('file-list');
            fileListDiv.innerHTML = '';
            for (var i = 0; i < input.files.length; i++) {
                fileListDiv.innerHTML += '<p>' + input.files[i].name + '</p>';
            }
        }

        document.getElementById('claim-form').addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
            event.preventDefault();
            document.getElementById('claim-form').style.display = 'none';
            var refNumber = 'MS-2026-08-' + Math.random().toString().slice(2, 6);
            document.getElementById('reference-number').innerText = refNumber;
            document.getElementById('confirmation').style.display = 'block';
            console.log('Analytics: Click on Submit Claim');
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>


Acceptance criteria:
- US-7-AC1: Given the landing page, when an advisor views the page, then a view event is recorded in analytics without personal identifiable information.
- US-7-AC2: Given the landing page, when an advisor clicks on a call to action, then a click event is recorded in analytics without revealing advisor identity.

Write pytest tests (a single test_app.py) that verify the happy path
STRUCTURALLY against the actual file above — read index.html from
Path(__file__).parent and assert what the criteria need: the form and its
required field ids exist, the upload input allows multiple files, the
confirmation panel and status markup exist, the member lookup mock data is
present. 4 to 6 focused tests, stdlib + pytest only, no browser, no server,
no network. Every assertion must hold for the file exactly as shown above,
and must be independent of the current date, time, or environment — never
hard-code a year, month, or timestamp; where the page generates a value at
runtime, assert the generating code exists, not the value it would produce
today.

JSON schema: {"files": [{"path": "test_app.py", "content": str}]}

